1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,480
 If you're going to make your first $100,000, it's not going to come from investing, and that's

2
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:08,120
 something that people don't get. Pretend you get average gains in the market of 8% per year and

3
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:14,080
 start with $10,000. It would still take you 30 years to hit $100,000 just investing that sum,

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:18,000
 and nobody wants to wait that long. Charlie Munger, who was Warren Buffett's right-hand man,

5
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:22,980
 said it best, the first $100,000 is a bitch, but you got to do it. I don't care what you have to do.

6
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:28,360
 So your first $100,000 actually comes mostly from saving every dollar and investing on top of that.

7
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:33,960
 If you save $12,000 a year for seven years at a 4.5% return, you will have $100,000. But look,

8
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:39,020
 84% of it came from savings, and only 16% of it came from the interest in gains.

9
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:43,320
 A lot of the friction in building wealth is at the beginning of the journey. So

10
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:47,360
 every dollar when you're starting out saving matters that much more. I hope this helps.

